1
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

2
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,763
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

3
00:00:54,846 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

4
00:00:58,058 --> 00:01:05,023
HOUSE OF GRACE

5
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,953
<i>The house where</i>
<i>my wife was born and raised.</i>

6
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,663
POSTS
dr.min.jh

7
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:22,958
<i>My mother-in-law always welcomes me</i>
<i>with open arms.</i>

8
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:54,740
Have some. You've come such a long way.

9
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:57,743
- Thank you.
- No problem.

10
00:01:58,702 --> 00:01:59,703
So…

11
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:03,832
how did you say you knew Eunhye?

12
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:10,630
Oh, I've never actually met
Ms. Joo Eunhye.

13
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:12,299
I…

14
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,469
know Mr. Min Junho and Hyunsoo.

15
00:02:16,053 --> 00:02:17,471
I see.

16
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:20,432
Please, have a seat.

17
00:02:27,606 --> 00:02:29,900
Your daughter was very beautiful.

18
00:02:32,361 --> 00:02:33,570
Yes, she was.

19
00:02:34,196 --> 00:02:35,656
She had such a gentle heart too.

20
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:45,582
Looks like your daughter
liked to cook too.

21
00:02:46,249 --> 00:02:48,168
The friend next to her is a chef.

22
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:53,757
They grew up in the same neighborhood
and were inseparable even into adulthood.

23
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:58,220
They even opened a restaurant together,

24
00:02:59,221 --> 00:03:02,599
but Eunhye left when she got married.

25
00:03:03,809 --> 00:03:04,810
Why?

26
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:09,439
Running a business just wasn't for her.

27
00:03:09,523 --> 00:03:11,733
Her dream was to be
a traditional wife and mother.

28
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:13,777
I see.

29
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:21,201
Well, anyway, what brings you here?

30
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:23,578
Oh, well…

31
00:03:24,913 --> 00:03:26,957
I'm not sure how to say this…

32
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,418
It's okay. Just tell me.

33
00:03:30,127 --> 00:03:31,795
You can be honest with me.

34
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:43,390
Not long ago, Mr. Min Junho and I…

35
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:46,726
went on a date.

36
00:04:02,367 --> 00:04:03,368
That's good to hear.

37
00:04:10,459 --> 00:04:11,460
That night…

38
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:15,130
it was raining really hard.

39
00:04:17,215 --> 00:04:20,719
<i>So because of the rain that night,</i>

40
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:24,181
<i>he came into my place</i>
<i>while he was waiting for his taxi.</i>

41
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:26,016
Hold on.

42
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:31,563
I'd rather not hear about the two of you.

43
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,023
When the time is right…

44
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:38,695
I'm sure he'll tell me himself.

45
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:45,869
Actually…

46
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:54,544
Never mind.

47
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:04,763
I just want to know
what Mr. Min was like back then.

48
00:05:09,601 --> 00:05:12,896
<i>Junho was absolutely devoted to Eunhye.</i>

49
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:16,942
He couldn't have treated her any better.

50
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:22,155
He was the best father to Hyunsoo,

51
00:05:22,948 --> 00:05:26,201
and he was a wonderful
son-in-law to us too.

52
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:34,876
Were he and Eunhye happy together
throughout their marriage?

53
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,089
<i>He was always a family man,</i>

54
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:41,967
<i>the kind of person</i>
<i>who only had eyes for his wife.</i>

55
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:45,053
Even when Eunhye was sick…

56
00:05:54,688 --> 00:05:58,525
I heard your daughter had
some unfortunate health issues.

57
00:06:02,946 --> 00:06:05,824
Could I ask if it got worse

58
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:08,034
after she got married?

59
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:11,496
I'd rather not talk about that anymore.

60
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,582
But didn't you find it a little strange?

61
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:15,709
I mean, her husband was a doctor,

62
00:06:15,792 --> 00:06:17,919
so for her to end up like that
from an overdose…

63
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:25,010
Are you implying my son-in-law
did something to my daughter?

64
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:28,346
No, that's not what I…

65
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:34,144
I'd like you to leave now.

66
00:06:48,617 --> 00:06:50,535
I'm sorry if I made you uncomfortable.

67
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:37,999
EPISODE 5
M

68
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:46,257
Jeongmi runs a café
in the theme park across the main road.

69
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:49,636
I guess it must be doing pretty well

70
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:52,180
if she's still in business
after all these years.

71
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:56,393
What's the place called?

72
00:07:57,894 --> 00:08:01,439
<i>Dear My Friend, I think.</i>

73
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:11,491
- Welcome.
- Hello.

74
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:14,160
Can I take your order?

75
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,831
Could I ask if the owner here…

76
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:25,505
Jeongmi?

77
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:33,722
You can't believe Min Junho
would do something like that, can you?

78
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:36,975
But…

79
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:42,397
I don't think you would've come
all this way just to lie about it.

80
00:08:46,735 --> 00:08:49,946
But why did you come to see me?

81
00:08:52,824 --> 00:08:55,660
I came because I wanted to
know more about Min Junho.

82
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:00,832
And about Ms. Joo Eunhye too.

83
00:09:03,126 --> 00:09:04,127
Eunhye?

84
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:11,551
I heard she died from an overdose.

85
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:16,931
Eunhye suffered from depression.

86
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,603
What was their marriage like?

87
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:29,986
They were much happier than most couples.

88
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,449
He was always so loving
and devoted to her.

89
00:09:35,617 --> 00:09:37,952
It was almost touching.

90
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:40,371
But Ms. Joo Eunhye wasn't happy, was she?

91
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:46,086
Maybe there was a problem
in their marriage

92
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:47,629
that she couldn't talk about?

93
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:53,134
-I don't think so--
-Was there ever anything

94
00:09:53,218 --> 00:09:55,053
that seemed strange or bothered you?

95
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:00,391
No.

96
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:04,187
You've known Eunhye
since you were very young.

97
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:08,691
Is there really nothing you can tell me?

98
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,568
Oh, gosh.

99
00:10:11,361 --> 00:10:12,612
I'm sorry.

100
00:10:23,790 --> 00:10:26,584
If you think of anything at all,
please call me anytime.

101
00:12:58,111 --> 00:13:03,074
Before Eunhye died…

102
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,121
Min Junho and I…

103
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:14,335
slept together.

104
00:13:18,464 --> 00:13:22,385
I'm not that kind of person.

105
00:13:24,095 --> 00:13:27,223
You have no idea how much
the guilt has been eating me alive.

106
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:38,026
All this time,
I thought it was all my fault.

107
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:47,285
You were drugged
with GHB too, weren't you?

108
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,498
I think so.

109
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:57,086
I felt sick all day the next day,

110
00:13:57,879 --> 00:14:00,381
and I couldn't remember anything.

111
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:07,055
It was the biggest mistake of my life.

112
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:12,685
After all this time…

113
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:17,148
It's pathetic, isn't it?

114
00:14:22,945 --> 00:14:24,572
It's the murder of the soul.

115
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:28,576
<i>You've been the victim</i>

116
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:30,870
<i>of one of the most heinous</i>
<i>and despicable crimes.</i>

117
00:14:34,165 --> 00:14:36,793
<i>Yet most victims believe</i>
<i>that they are the ones at fault.</i>

118
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:41,881
<i>They endlessly torture themselves</i>
<i>with regret and blame.</i>

119
00:14:45,927 --> 00:14:49,514
<i>Even after they realize what happened,</i>
<i>very few ever report it.</i>

120
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:57,647
I was the same way.

121
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,363
I don't know how, but…

122
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:08,825
Eunhye…

123
00:15:11,786 --> 00:15:15,123
found out about what happened
between Min Junho and me.

124
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:19,836
And after that…

125
00:15:23,714 --> 00:15:25,508
Not long after…

126
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:28,386
Eunhye…

127
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:36,477
It wasn't your fault, Jeongmi.

128
00:15:36,561 --> 00:15:38,479
Eunhye must have also known the truth

129
00:15:38,563 --> 00:15:40,648
about what kind of person
Min Junho really was.

130
00:15:44,318 --> 00:15:45,778
Come to Sangcheon with me.

131
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:49,198
I hope you can go to the police
and tell them the truth,

132
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:52,910
and let people know
what kind of person Min Junho really is.

133
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,288
Okay.

134
00:15:59,834 --> 00:16:01,961
-Really?
-Yes.

135
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:05,298
I feel like it has to be done.

136
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:26,360
ALL RECORDINGS

137
00:16:29,488 --> 00:16:31,991
KIM JEONGMI STATEMENT

138
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:38,206
DETECTIVE LEE HWAYOUNG
KIM JEONGMI STATEMENT.m4a

139
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:04,982
CALLING
KIM JEONGMI

140
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:08,778
<i>The call cannot be connected.</i>

141
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:10,738
<i>Please leave a message after the…</i>

142
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:17,954
<i>The call cannot be connected.</i>

143
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:21,123
<i>Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

144
00:18:02,039 --> 00:18:06,043
A good scalpel cuts so cleanly
that it doesn't even leave a trace.

145
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:08,337
Then, a moment later,

146
00:18:08,421 --> 00:18:11,215
a gasp of admiration bursts out
at just how perfect the cut was.

147
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,720
And that gasp comes in the form of blood.

148
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,607
-Hello?
-Sorry to call so early.

149
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,233
Did you listen to the recording?

150
00:18:31,694 --> 00:18:33,029
What recording?

151
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:34,655
I sent it last night.

152
00:18:35,865 --> 00:18:39,744
Min Junho used GHB
to assault his late wife's friend too.

153
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:41,162
The same method he used on me.

154
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:45,416
Wait. You were supposed to
keep your distance from Min Junho.

155
00:18:45,499 --> 00:18:48,753
We agreed to go to the police together,
but now I can't get a hold of her.

156
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:55,593
Let me listen to the recording first.
I'll call you back.

157
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:06,979
<i>I felt sick all day the next day,</i>

158
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:10,316
<i>and I couldn't remember anything.</i>

159
00:19:11,067 --> 00:19:13,361
<i>I thought it was just a hangover, but…</i>

160
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:20,618
<i>It was the biggest mistake of my life.</i>

161
00:19:25,164 --> 00:19:26,290
Saw.

162
00:19:32,505 --> 00:19:34,965
We have new evidence,
so you can reinvestigate, right?

163
00:19:35,925 --> 00:19:37,301
This would open a new case.

164
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:41,681
She can report it herself,
but it isn't evidence that would justify

165
00:19:41,764 --> 00:19:43,557
reopening a previous investigation.

166
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:44,809
That makes no sense.

167
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,769
I wasn't Min Junho's first victim!

168
00:19:49,021 --> 00:19:51,065
<i>A recording of her statement</i>
<i>isn't enough</i>

169
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:53,526
<i>if she doesn't come forward herself.</i>
<i>Besides…</i>

170
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:57,405
She doesn't have any evidence either,
does she?

171
00:20:25,099 --> 00:20:26,517
Heart, please.

172
00:22:23,759 --> 00:22:25,553
You said you had some bleeding?

173
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:26,887
Yes.

174
00:22:26,971 --> 00:22:28,722
I was fine until yesterday.

175
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:31,100
You're ten weeks pregnant.

176
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:33,769
Don't worry.

177
00:22:33,853 --> 00:22:37,064
Some light bleeding is common
at this stage of pregnancy.

178
00:22:37,690 --> 00:22:40,693
But I'm sure you're still worried,
so let's take a look at the baby.

179
00:22:40,776 --> 00:22:42,736
Yes, and for some reason…

180
00:22:43,946 --> 00:22:46,448
…I'm experiencing acute pain down there.

181
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:52,204
See the heartbeat here?

182
00:22:52,288 --> 00:22:54,415
The baby's healthy and growing well.

183
00:22:59,336 --> 00:23:01,338
I'll print out a copy for you.

184
00:23:01,422 --> 00:23:02,548
Thank you.

185
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:08,178
Oh, and I noticed some abrasions inside.

186
00:23:08,262 --> 00:23:09,805
There are a few of them.

187
00:23:09,889 --> 00:23:12,266
They seem to be
what's causing the bleeding and pain.

188
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:15,311
That can't be…

189
00:23:15,978 --> 00:23:19,273
Abrasions like that
can sometimes happen during sex.

190
00:23:20,065 --> 00:23:22,651
They'll probably heal over time,

191
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:25,654
but you might want to
talk to your husband about it.

192
00:23:26,906 --> 00:23:27,907
No, I…

193
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:39,793
I…

194
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:43,130
I'd like to have some blood drawn, please.

195
00:25:40,664 --> 00:25:42,249
SUNDAY

196
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:56,305
THURSDAY

197
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:08,317
Hey, it's me.

198
00:26:09,193 --> 00:26:11,445
Did you find out
who the car is registered to?

199
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:14,698
<i>Oh. I called several times</i>
<i>yesterday, but you--</i>

200
00:26:14,782 --> 00:26:16,325
So who's the car owner?

201
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,910
<i>Min Junho.</i>

202
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:20,704
<i>The doctor.</i>

203
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:39,241
<i>I feel like it has to be done.</i>

204
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:42,452
I have to do it for my friend Eunhye.

205
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:48,208
It's the anniversary of her death
in two days.

206
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:02,347
I'll take that.

207
00:28:54,358 --> 00:28:55,692
Oh.

208
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,236
Sir, wait!

209
00:30:07,514 --> 00:30:10,183
We agreed we'd go to Sangcheon together.

210
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:16,273
I think I rushed you
into making that decision.

211
00:30:18,984 --> 00:30:21,445
I don't have any reason to go there.

212
00:30:23,905 --> 00:30:26,533
It's okay.
Take your time to think about it.

213
00:30:26,616 --> 00:30:29,369
You can just talk to the police
over the phone too.

214
00:30:29,453 --> 00:30:33,790
I do feel terrible about
what you say happened to you,

215
00:30:33,874 --> 00:30:36,084
whether it's true or not.

216
00:30:36,835 --> 00:30:40,213
But what happened to you
and what happened to me aren't the same.

217
00:30:45,427 --> 00:30:47,512
Did something happen?

218
00:30:49,598 --> 00:30:53,643
Everything I told you the other day…

219
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:58,065
was a lie.

220
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:00,901
I'm sorry.

221
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,738
I hated myself for getting drunk

222
00:31:04,821 --> 00:31:07,449
and making that mistake
with my friend's husband,

223
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:09,951
then losing my friend.

224
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:14,081
I wanted to ease some of the guilt--

225
00:31:14,164 --> 00:31:16,416
This isn't how you were the other day.

226
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:20,128
You knew exactly how dangerous
and evil Min Junho was.

227
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:22,422
So why are you suddenly…

228
00:31:22,506 --> 00:31:24,758
Oh, gosh.

229
00:31:25,801 --> 00:31:27,761
Oh, yes, Junho.

230
00:31:29,054 --> 00:31:30,847
Sorry to keep you waiting.

231
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:33,600
Could you and Eunhye's mother
wait in the car?

232
00:31:35,185 --> 00:31:37,521
Okay. I'll be right out.

233
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,191
I have to go.

234
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:47,155
You're afraid of Min Junho, aren't you?

235
00:31:50,534 --> 00:31:53,954
What are you talking about?

236
00:31:55,914 --> 00:31:58,333
Junho is a good person.

237
00:31:59,459 --> 00:32:02,546
I was the one
who developed feelings for him.

238
00:32:04,548 --> 00:32:05,841
I kept pursuing him.

239
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:10,595
I'm the one who caused him
to make that mistake.

240
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:19,271
Can you swear to that
in front of Ms. Joo Eunhye?

241
00:32:24,067 --> 00:32:27,696
You're incredibly rude and invasive.

242
00:32:28,697 --> 00:32:31,825
Stop harassing people
who just want to be left alone.

243
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:34,202
Before I call the police.

244
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:36,079
Jeongmi.

245
00:32:42,961 --> 00:32:44,713
It wasn't your fault.

246
00:33:02,272 --> 00:33:04,524
<i>Attention, please.</i>

247
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:10,906
<i>Flight 7C55 to Sangcheon has been</i>
<i>canceled due to weather conditions.</i>

248
00:33:11,948 --> 00:33:14,075
<i>Once again,</i>

249
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:20,498
<i>flight 7C55 to Sangcheon has been</i>
<i>canceled due to weather conditions.</i>

250
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:23,335
<i>We apologize for the inconvenience.</i>

251
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,128
<i>Thank you.</i>

252
00:33:25,212 --> 00:33:26,963
<i> Attention, please…</i>

253
00:33:30,717 --> 00:33:32,969
WHITE PSYCHIATRIC CLINIC

254
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:36,556
It's been three years already.

255
00:33:38,225 --> 00:33:40,268
And yet here I am, still a mess.

256
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:42,103
What's wrong with me?

257
00:33:43,897 --> 00:33:47,525
Even when I try to make a fresh start,
I end up with some attention seeker.

258
00:33:47,609 --> 00:33:49,945
I keep telling you, it's not your fault.

259
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:53,031
Sometimes… I think…

260
00:33:55,700 --> 00:33:57,369
"I don't want to live anymore."

261
00:33:58,411 --> 00:33:59,829
"I miss Eunhye."

262
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,961
Will a two-week prescription be enough?

263
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:12,592
I'll need a medical certificate too.

264
00:34:14,511 --> 00:34:16,763
HOTEL PARKING ENTRANCE
KEEP ENTRANCE AND EXIT CLEAR

265
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:21,142
<i>You're going to sue that woman?</i>

266
00:34:23,353 --> 00:34:24,354
<i>Yeah.</i>

267
00:34:26,022 --> 00:34:28,858
<i>Make sure you're legally covered</i>
<i>to avoid problems down the road.</i>

268
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:33,738
Welcome.

269
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:35,073
Are you with a party?

270
00:34:35,699 --> 00:34:36,992
No, it's just me.

271
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:39,911
In that case,
would you mind sitting at the bar?

272
00:34:39,995 --> 00:34:41,246
Not at all.

273
00:34:41,329 --> 00:34:42,372
Great. Right this way.

274
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,231
What can I get you?

275
00:35:09,399 --> 00:35:10,525
A dark beer, please.

276
00:35:10,609 --> 00:35:12,110
Sure.

277
00:35:12,193 --> 00:35:13,194
Oh.

278
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:16,740
I'll just have one of these.

279
00:35:16,823 --> 00:35:18,199
Sure, okay.

280
00:35:29,711 --> 00:35:31,421
Here you go.

281
00:35:37,636 --> 00:35:40,263
I guess we can just switch ourselves.

282
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,931
Okay.

283
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:49,564
I've been coming here
for over three years,

284
00:35:50,357 --> 00:35:52,192
and they still don't know what I drink.

285
00:36:11,670 --> 00:36:12,671
Excuse…

286
00:36:13,380 --> 00:36:14,631
Excuse me…

287
00:36:16,257 --> 00:36:18,468
- We'd like to order, please!
- Oh, yes.

288
00:36:22,639 --> 00:36:24,015
What can I get you?

289
00:36:24,099 --> 00:36:25,850
I'll have another one of these, please.

290
00:36:25,934 --> 00:36:27,185
Sure.

291
00:36:35,026 --> 00:36:37,278
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

292
00:36:52,502 --> 00:36:53,628
If it's okay with you,

293
00:36:54,587 --> 00:36:57,674
would you like me to recommend
a good hangover soup place nearby?

294
00:37:26,619 --> 00:37:28,371
Want another drink?

295
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:29,831
This one's on me.

296
00:37:30,665 --> 00:37:32,041
No, actually…

297
00:37:32,959 --> 00:37:35,962
How about we share a bottle of wine?

298
00:37:49,768 --> 00:37:50,935
I should get going.

299
00:37:51,895 --> 00:37:53,271
What?

300
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:55,899
-Wait, how about a glass of--
-I said no.

301
00:38:07,494 --> 00:38:08,495
Hey.

302
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,041
Hey.

303
00:38:13,917 --> 00:38:15,251
Hey, wait.

304
00:38:16,503 --> 00:38:17,962
Wait! Hey.

305
00:38:21,216 --> 00:38:23,176
-Wait--
-Don't touch me!

306
00:38:34,354 --> 00:38:37,482
You left your phone.

307
00:39:16,271 --> 00:39:17,397
Hello?

308
00:39:20,358 --> 00:39:22,610
<i>This is the</i>
<i>Forensic Science Department at the NFS.</i>

309
00:39:23,945 --> 00:39:26,155
<i>The GHB test you requested…</i>

310
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,284
<i>We have the results, and…</i>

311
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:31,744
4. RESULTS OF ANALYSIS
GAMMA-HYDROXYBUTYRIC ACID, GHB

312
00:39:31,828 --> 00:39:32,871
POSITIVE

313
00:39:32,954 --> 00:39:34,205
<i>It came back positive.</i>

314
00:39:38,543 --> 00:39:40,295
<i>Hello, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

315
00:39:41,629 --> 00:39:46,134
<i>This is your captain, Kang Ilcheon.</i>

316
00:39:47,510 --> 00:39:50,179
<i>Thank you for flying with us</i>
<i>on Air Donghae Flight 701</i>

317
00:39:50,263 --> 00:39:52,056
<i>to Sangcheon Airport.</i>

318
00:39:54,017 --> 00:39:56,144
<i>The weather in Sangcheon</i>
<i>is currently clear,</i>

319
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:58,980
<i>with a temperature of 25 degrees Celsius.</i>

320
00:39:59,063 --> 00:40:03,902
<i>The weather in Sangcheon</i>
<i>is expected to remain mild today,</i>

321
00:40:03,985 --> 00:40:05,820
<i>but unexpected changes in air currents</i>

322
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:08,031
<i>may cause severe turbulence.</i>

323
00:40:09,198 --> 00:40:10,617
What a coincidence.

324
00:40:11,326 --> 00:40:13,202
Well, I guess not.

325
00:40:13,286 --> 00:40:16,789
We did both say
we were going to Sangcheon.

326
00:40:20,877 --> 00:40:22,253
If you're uncomfortable,

327
00:40:23,338 --> 00:40:26,341
should I ask to switch seats?

328
00:40:28,801 --> 00:40:30,553
No, it's fine. You can stay.

329
00:40:43,775 --> 00:40:44,859
It was good, right?

330
00:40:46,027 --> 00:40:47,028
Sorry?

331
00:40:49,113 --> 00:40:50,782
The hangover soup place.

332
00:40:53,493 --> 00:40:57,080
-I didn't have time to go.
-Ah.

333
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:02,543
Well, next time you're there,
you should definitely try it.

334
00:41:02,627 --> 00:41:04,045
You won't regret it.

335
00:41:07,799 --> 00:41:08,800
Okay.

336
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:15,932
You know,

337
00:41:17,100 --> 00:41:19,185
I'm not usually like that.

338
00:41:21,688 --> 00:41:22,689
Sorry?

339
00:41:23,815 --> 00:41:24,816
I just…

340
00:41:25,900 --> 00:41:29,570
don't want you to think
I'm some kind of creep.

341
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:33,032
I don't normally

342
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:40,081
ask women I just met at a bar
to have a drink with me.

343
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,458
That's really not who I am.

344
00:41:44,002 --> 00:41:46,337
Ah. Okay.

345
00:41:48,089 --> 00:41:50,800
I don't know
if I should ask you this, but…

346
00:41:52,552 --> 00:41:56,139
was it because you have a boyfriend?

347
00:42:00,393 --> 00:42:03,062
No, but…

348
00:42:06,482 --> 00:42:07,525
Ah.

349
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:11,487
It's okay. Really.

350
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:17,201
Could you, then…

351
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:20,997
give me some advice?

352
00:42:21,873 --> 00:42:23,583
What did I do to put you off?

353
00:42:23,666 --> 00:42:25,418
You didn't do anything wrong.

354
00:42:28,046 --> 00:42:29,505
It's just…

355
00:42:32,300 --> 00:42:34,927
I'm just not in a position
to date anyone right now.

356
00:42:44,437 --> 00:42:47,231
I don't know what you're going through…

357
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:54,781
but I hope everything works out for you.

358
00:42:57,033 --> 00:42:58,159
Thank you.

359
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:24,727
Have you ever been through
something like this?

360
00:43:29,357 --> 00:43:30,900
Something happens,

361
00:43:32,068 --> 00:43:34,153
and overnight,

362
00:43:34,237 --> 00:43:36,072
it's like your whole world has changed.

363
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:41,410
You didn't do anything wrong,

364
00:43:42,495 --> 00:43:44,539
but somehow you're the one
everyone shuts out.

365
00:43:46,999 --> 00:43:48,668
You don't know what to do…

366
00:43:50,670 --> 00:43:55,216
and you have no idea how to get back
to the way things were before.

367
00:43:59,929 --> 00:44:03,099
It might be better to accept
your new reality sooner rather than later…

368
00:44:05,476 --> 00:44:08,896
-and learn to adjust to it.
-You're telling me to just accept it?

369
00:44:13,276 --> 00:44:16,070
I found that the more I tried
to go back to the way things were…

370
00:44:17,947 --> 00:44:19,657
the more it hurt.

371
00:44:27,707 --> 00:44:29,458
It's better to make your new reality…

372
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:34,130
feel as familiar as you can.

373
00:44:37,258 --> 00:44:40,344
Because familiarity gives you
a sense of security.

374
00:44:47,727 --> 00:44:50,605
It's the least painful way

375
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:54,108
to recover as quickly as possible.

376
00:45:22,595 --> 00:45:24,472
Well, then, take care.

377
00:45:27,475 --> 00:45:28,476
Wait.

378
00:45:33,064 --> 00:45:34,482
Do you want to grab a bite?

379
00:45:40,238 --> 00:45:42,406
Let me treat you to dinner.

380
00:45:42,490 --> 00:45:44,242
When are you free?

381
00:45:57,380 --> 00:45:58,714
Why me?

382
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:10,017
I just thought it'd be nice
to have a meal together.

383
00:46:11,143 --> 00:46:12,520
And after that?

384
00:46:20,069 --> 00:46:23,781
If you're not interested,
you can just say no.

385
00:46:27,034 --> 00:46:28,035
Well, then…

386
00:46:29,870 --> 00:46:31,080
Take care.

387
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:46,595
So I told her to invite her friends,

388
00:46:46,679 --> 00:46:50,182
and she asked if they
couldn't just hang out by themselves.

389
00:46:50,266 --> 00:46:52,435
Basically, she just wanted my credit card.

390
00:46:52,518 --> 00:46:53,936
So you know what I told her?

391
00:46:54,478 --> 00:46:58,482
"Sweetheart, family dinner comes first."

392
00:47:02,778 --> 00:47:03,904
Inspector Lee.

393
00:47:04,739 --> 00:47:05,740
Yes, sir.

394
00:47:05,823 --> 00:47:06,866
You okay?

395
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:08,659
Yes.

396
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:11,912
Why are you looking at that?

397
00:47:13,622 --> 00:47:15,041
I have to testify in court.

398
00:47:15,750 --> 00:47:17,460
Oh, that's right.

399
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:22,256
Kids these days
are scarier than adults, huh?

400
00:47:24,383 --> 00:47:27,595
So, you're telling me
it's just because of the case?

401
00:47:31,015 --> 00:47:33,184
You seem like your mind's
somewhere else today.

402
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:36,437
If GHB was detected,

403
00:47:37,813 --> 00:47:40,024
we have to find out who did it.

404
00:47:41,400 --> 00:47:43,319
Even if the circumstances
point to someone,

405
00:47:43,402 --> 00:47:45,529
we still need proof
that it was that person.

406
00:47:52,787 --> 00:47:53,829
Never mind.

407
00:47:57,291 --> 00:47:59,377
Inspector Lee.

408
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:03,964
You know you can talk to me
about anything, right?

409
00:48:04,715 --> 00:48:07,843
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?
You're making me uncomfortable.

410
00:48:17,353 --> 00:48:18,646
Huh?

411
00:48:32,535 --> 00:48:33,994
<i> This is Sangcheon Police.</i>

412
00:48:34,078 --> 00:48:37,915
<i>A complaint has been filed against you</i>
<i>for false accusation and defamation.</i>

413
00:49:02,148 --> 00:49:03,941
How dare you file a complaint against me?

414
00:49:05,734 --> 00:49:08,779
You're only making things worse
for yourself by doing this here.

415
00:49:09,697 --> 00:49:11,657
If you need a lawyer, I can recommend one.

416
00:49:11,740 --> 00:49:13,492
Defamation?

417
00:49:13,576 --> 00:49:14,869
False accusation?

418
00:49:14,952 --> 00:49:17,121
You have the nerve to do this
after what you did?

419
00:49:17,204 --> 00:49:18,581
I've been falsely accused.

420
00:49:18,664 --> 00:49:20,332
I can't just let that go.

421
00:49:21,709 --> 00:49:23,043
"Falsely accused"?

422
00:49:24,587 --> 00:49:27,006
Have you ever been honest
with anyone in your life?

423
00:49:31,177 --> 00:49:33,095
I understand how you feel.

424
00:49:34,221 --> 00:49:36,348
And I know what you think of me.

425
00:49:43,731 --> 00:49:44,732
So?

426
00:49:45,733 --> 00:49:46,984
What are you going to do?

427
00:49:59,788 --> 00:50:03,792
Honestly, don't you just
want to put an end to all this…

428
00:50:05,461 --> 00:50:07,963
and go back to living
a quiet, normal life like before?

429
00:50:10,132 --> 00:50:11,133
Hmm?

430
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:13,511
You should go back.

431
00:50:15,137 --> 00:50:16,222
To the way things were.

432
00:50:17,640 --> 00:50:18,641
Hmm?

433
00:50:22,478 --> 00:50:24,313
I'll give you a chance to start over.

434
00:50:27,233 --> 00:50:28,567
It's easier than you think.

435
00:50:30,277 --> 00:50:31,987
All you have to do

436
00:50:32,071 --> 00:50:34,406
is post that you made the whole thing up
to frame me.

437
00:50:35,699 --> 00:50:39,620
With sincere remorse and an apology.

438
00:50:41,914 --> 00:50:44,250
You want me to lie for you?

439
00:50:49,797 --> 00:50:52,883
Is this how you threatened
and manipulated Kim Jeongmi too?

440
00:50:55,761 --> 00:50:58,514
I'm never going to give in.

441
00:51:01,642 --> 00:51:02,643
You…

442
00:51:04,103 --> 00:51:08,148
disrespected me
and tarnished my reputation.

443
00:51:17,616 --> 00:51:18,909
So that's what this is about.

444
00:51:23,914 --> 00:51:25,416
You rapist!

445
00:51:26,792 --> 00:51:29,628
Min Junho is a rapist!

446
00:51:34,842 --> 00:51:37,970
Why don't we go inside
instead of doing this out here?

447
00:51:48,897 --> 00:51:50,107
Keep quiet,

448
00:51:51,150 --> 00:51:54,528
or you'll disappear right here.

449
00:52:46,705 --> 00:52:48,707
DNA ANALYSIS RESULTS NOTICE

450
00:53:02,638 --> 00:53:06,392
THE DNA PROFILE OF THE VICTIM,
LEE HWAYOUNG, WAS DETECTED,

451
00:53:06,475 --> 00:53:09,603
AND NO OTHER DNA PROFILES WERE DETECTED

452
00:53:09,687 --> 00:53:11,397
SANGCHEON POLICE STATION

453
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:12,481
Ma'am.

454
00:53:13,148 --> 00:53:14,191
Detective.

455
00:53:14,274 --> 00:53:16,819
Can't you testify without my son?

456
00:53:18,654 --> 00:53:20,531
What do you mean?

457
00:53:23,283 --> 00:53:25,119
My son…

458
00:53:25,202 --> 00:53:26,537
I think he's scared.

459
00:53:27,329 --> 00:53:30,708
We don't know when those guys
might come after him again.

460
00:53:35,087 --> 00:53:36,922
Let me talk to him.

461
00:53:41,343 --> 00:53:42,594
Hi, Chowon.

462
00:53:45,681 --> 00:53:46,974
Are you upset?

463
00:53:53,605 --> 00:53:55,482
You don't think you can testify?

464
00:54:02,656 --> 00:54:03,657
No.

465
00:54:11,331 --> 00:54:13,667
Remember what you told me before?

466
00:54:15,335 --> 00:54:17,463
You asked me to make sure
those guys were caught.

467
00:54:19,631 --> 00:54:21,800
So they could never
do something like that again.

468
00:54:25,512 --> 00:54:27,556
Do you remember what I told you then?

469
00:54:31,310 --> 00:54:32,603
I told you…

470
00:54:35,439 --> 00:54:37,649
that you had to be brave…

471
00:54:40,360 --> 00:54:42,196
if you wanted them to be punished.

472
00:54:45,324 --> 00:54:47,284
If you don't say anything…

473
00:54:50,704 --> 00:54:53,040
and keep what happened to yourself…

474
00:54:56,752 --> 00:54:58,712
you might regret it someday.

475
00:55:04,718 --> 00:55:06,345
Are you okay?

476
00:55:12,726 --> 00:55:18,524
dr.min.jh
MIN JUNHO

477
00:55:30,911 --> 00:55:33,372
CAPTAIN

478
00:55:54,935 --> 00:55:55,936
CALLING
KANG JISUN

479
00:56:00,816 --> 00:56:03,777
<i>The call cannot be connected.</i>

480
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:06,446
<i>Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

481
00:56:14,121 --> 00:56:15,914
<i>Hey, Inspector Lee. What's up?</i>

482
00:56:16,540 --> 00:56:17,833
Sir.

483
00:56:19,418 --> 00:56:21,670
There's something important
I need to tell you.

484
00:56:26,383 --> 00:56:30,012
Let's arrest him today.
Let's throw that bastard in jail.

485
00:56:33,390 --> 00:56:35,434
We need to be extremely thorough first.

486
00:56:36,518 --> 00:56:38,020
If we fail to get him again…

487
00:56:41,815 --> 00:56:47,362
A positive GHB test alone
doesn't prove that bastard gave it to you.

488
00:56:47,446 --> 00:56:49,531
We need to dig up circumstantial evidence.

489
00:56:49,615 --> 00:56:52,826
We need his call records
and the location data from his car too.

490
00:56:52,909 --> 00:56:54,036
I'll put in the requests.

491
00:56:54,119 --> 00:56:56,204
I'll give them hell
until they take care of it.

492
00:56:59,207 --> 00:57:01,793
- Thank you for meeting me today.
- And this case…

493
00:57:03,420 --> 00:57:05,213
I'll take the lead on the investigation.

494
00:57:06,882 --> 00:57:09,384
I knew something felt off
about that bastard

495
00:57:09,468 --> 00:57:11,219
from the moment I saw his face.

496
00:57:17,559 --> 00:57:18,935
As for my husband…

497
00:57:22,064 --> 00:57:23,565
Please don't tell him.

498
00:57:26,026 --> 00:57:29,071
I guess Seokgu doesn't know.

499
00:57:29,738 --> 00:57:31,573
Just until we solve the case.

500
00:57:33,617 --> 00:57:34,618
Okay.

501
00:57:37,621 --> 00:57:39,414
We're going to get that bastard.

502
00:57:58,642 --> 00:57:59,851
- What the…
- Oh, my gosh.

503
00:57:59,935 --> 00:58:01,687
Oh, no. Is she hurt?

504
00:58:01,770 --> 00:58:03,397
She's had way too much to drink.

505
00:58:04,606 --> 00:58:05,774
Excuse me.

506
00:58:13,657 --> 00:58:14,866
I'm sorry.

507
00:58:26,253 --> 00:58:27,796
You said you wanted to start over.

508
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:31,591
Have you given up on everything?

509
00:58:41,685 --> 00:58:43,520
Where are you going? We need to talk.

510
00:58:46,273 --> 00:58:47,274
You're drunk.

511
00:58:53,238 --> 00:58:55,115
Min Junho!

512
00:58:58,160 --> 00:59:00,620
Min Junho!

513
00:59:06,251 --> 00:59:07,252
Make your choice.

514
00:59:07,919 --> 00:59:10,422
Either keep quiet or end it here.

515
00:59:10,505 --> 00:59:12,340
I won't need a lawyer.

516
00:59:18,638 --> 00:59:20,015
You win.

517
00:59:22,809 --> 00:59:24,269
I give up.

518
00:59:26,980 --> 00:59:30,859
I'll do whatever you want,
whatever you tell me to.

519
00:59:31,943 --> 00:59:34,154
So please, just let me live.

520
00:59:42,829 --> 00:59:44,206
You'd better keep your word.

521
00:59:52,506 --> 00:59:54,257
Sure thing.

522
01:00:08,313 --> 01:00:09,606
Damn it…

523
01:00:20,367 --> 01:00:22,577
Damn it, where are my keys?

524
01:00:26,915 --> 01:00:28,083
You're going to drive?

525
01:00:28,166 --> 01:00:29,167
Not your business.

526
01:00:47,894 --> 01:00:49,771
I can't, but you can, right?

527
01:00:52,107 --> 01:00:53,942
-What?
-Give me a ride.

528
01:00:59,114 --> 01:01:00,866
Don't you know what kind of person I am?

529
01:01:02,701 --> 01:01:04,870
You're the one who called me a criminal.

530
01:01:04,953 --> 01:01:06,830
Yeah, but you know what?

531
01:01:07,873 --> 01:01:10,125
I'm not scared of you at all.

532
01:01:11,960 --> 01:01:12,961
What about you?

533
01:01:14,713 --> 01:01:17,465
You're scared of women.

534
01:01:19,926 --> 01:01:22,220
What the heck made you this way?

535
01:01:24,389 --> 01:01:27,684
Were you starved for affection as a kid?

536
01:01:27,767 --> 01:01:29,060
Were you abused?

537
01:01:33,231 --> 01:01:34,232
Just go home quietly.

538
01:01:34,774 --> 01:01:36,359
And what if I don't?

539
01:01:41,907 --> 01:01:43,742
I told you to just go!

540
01:02:05,597 --> 01:02:07,766
What the…

541
01:02:09,476 --> 01:02:10,936
What's wrong?

542
01:02:11,645 --> 01:02:12,938
Are you okay?

543
01:02:20,070 --> 01:02:21,071
You…

544
01:02:34,834 --> 01:02:38,755
THE PERFECT LIE

545
01:03:04,906 --> 01:03:07,450
I'm not going to make
the same mistake this time.

546
01:03:08,284 --> 01:03:10,829
So this time,
I'm going to be the one lying.

547
01:03:10,912 --> 01:03:13,498
<i>What if I tell them</i>
<i>I was with you that day, Dad?</i>

548
01:03:13,581 --> 01:03:15,959
How do you know your dad didn't go out?

549
01:03:16,042 --> 01:03:18,795
I can't make you lie too.

550
01:03:18,878 --> 01:03:21,214
I guess the investigation
isn't going so well again.

551
01:03:21,297 --> 01:03:23,425
You don't need to know
everything about my work.

552
01:03:23,508 --> 01:03:26,011
<i>Min Junho isn't going to just let this go.</i>

553
01:03:26,094 --> 01:03:28,346
<i>He'll find some way to get back at me.</i>

554
01:03:46,072 --> 01:03:47,657
THE PERFECT LIE

555
01:03:47,741 --> 01:03:49,743
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
